    "sources": {
      "calibration_prose": "Orchard inventory: Mira counts seven green crates beside the east gate. Each crate holds twelve pears. After two crates leave on Tuesday, the remaining fruit is sorted by size and recorded in a notebook. Explain the stock changes carefully, distinguish fruit from containers, and preserve the order of events. The next delivery arrives after sunset, so its contents belong to a separate ledger entry.",
      "calibration_code": "def merge_counts(left, right):\n    result = dict(left)\n    for name, count in right.items():\n        if count < 0:\n            raise ValueError('negative inventory')\n        result[name] = result.get(name, 0) + count\n    return result\n\n# Review empty inputs, duplicate keys, and preservation of caller dictionaries.\n# State the expected result for {'a': 2} merged with {'a': 3, 'b': 1}.\n",
      "validation_prose": "Harbor timetable: the north ferry departs before the south ferry, while the cargo vessel waits for a pilot. Lidia writes the arrival times in blue ink and departure times in black. A cancelled trip receives its own note rather than erasing the original entry. Describe a procedure for checking this record, retaining uncertainty when a clock reading is missing, and keeping passengers distinct from cargo.",
      "validation_unicode": "\u041b\u0430\u0431\u043e\u0440\u0430\u0442\u043e\u0440\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u0436\u0443\u0440\u043d\u0430\u043b: \u0442\u0435\u043c\u043f\u0435\u0440\u0430\u0442\u0443\u0440\u0430 \u0432\u043e\u0434\u044b \u0440\u0430\u0432\u043d\u0430 18 \u00b0C, \u043c\u0430\u0441\u0441\u0430 \u043e\u0431\u0440\u0430\u0437\u0446\u0430 \u2014 2,5 \u0433. \u0418\u0441\u0441\u043b\u0435\u0434\u043e\u0432\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c \u0437\u0430\u043f\u0438\u0441\u044b\u0432\u0430\u0435\u0442 \u0432\u0440\u0435\u043c\u044f, \u0435\u0434\u0438\u043d\u0438\u0446\u044b \u0438\u0437\u043c\u0435\u0440\u0435\u043d\u0438\u044f \u0438 \u043f\u0440\u0438\u0447\u0438\u043d\u0443 \u043a\u0430\u0436\u0434\u043e\u0433\u043e \u043f\u043e\u0432\u0442\u043e\u0440\u043d\u043e\u0433\u043e \u043e\u043f\u044b\u0442\u0430. Compare these observations with a separate English summary. Preserve punctuation, decimal separators, and the distinction between an observation and a prediction. Symbols include \u03b1, \u03b2, \u00b1, and an arrow \u2192 between two labelled states.",
      "validation_code": "struct Queue { items: Vec<u32>, head: usize }\nimpl Queue {\n    fn pop(&mut self) -> Option<u32> {\n        let value = self.items.get(self.head).copied()?;\n        self.head += 1;\n        Some(value)\n    }\n}\n// Trace three successful calls and one empty call. Discuss indexing, ownership,\n// and how an error differs from exhaustion. Keep the examples deterministic.\n"
    },
